# Never let real credentials reach a build context that gets baked into an
# image layer (image layers are immutable and pushed to Artifact Registry —
# deleting the file afterward does NOT remove it from an already-pushed
# layer). This is the single most important rule in this file; see the risk
# assessment that led to it. Cloud Run gets its secrets at deploy time via
# --set-secrets / --set-env-vars, never via a file copied into the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*service-account*.json
*-key.json
firestore-key*.json
**/chaveGCP/**

# VCS / editor / OS cruft
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python build/test artifacts — never needed at runtime
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/

# Node — node_modules is rebuilt inside the image from package-lock.json
# (reproducible, correct platform/arch); shipping a host-built copy here
# would fight that and can bake in the wrong platform's native binaries.
node_calc/node_modules/

# Tests, benchmark tooling and its (large, run-specific) output, docs,
# deployment artifacts for the OTHER (chaos-sync) container — none of this
# is imported by the running app; shipping it only costs image size and
# surface area.
tests/
scripts/faithfulness_benchmark/out/
.github/
*.bundle
*.patch
data/replays/
CLAUDE.md
README.md
DATA.md
